# Detective Mosa — .gitignore
#
# Internal docs are hidden by DYNAMIC WHITELIST (ignore-everything-except),
# never by naming them individually — GIT.md §1. That rule protects itself:
# do not add explicit lines naming any internal doc or tool-config directory.

# --- Root-level internal docs (dynamic whitelist: everything but README.md) ---
/*.md
!/README.md

# --- Root-level internal dot-directories (dynamic whitelist: everything but .github/) ---
# Also covers the Godot 4 import cache (.godot/) and the legacy Godot 3
# import folder (.import/) as a side effect — both belong here anyway.
/.*/
!/.github/

# --- Internal working folders ---
/context/
/tickets/
/design/
/art/source/

# --- Internal root files not caught by the whitelists above ---
.gitmessage
*.pdf

# --- Godot: engine + import cache already covered by the dot-dir whitelist ---

# --- Godot: Android export secrets — never committed ---
/export_presets.cfg
*.keystore
*.jks
/android/build/

# --- Build output — regenerable, and APKs are large binaries ---
/build/

# --- Godot: generated/derived, safe to rebuild ---
*.translation
*.tmp

# NOTE: *.import files are intentionally NOT ignored — Godot needs them to
# resolve assets, and every teammate's clone breaks without them (GIT.md §3).
